      "id": "math-i-limits-algebraic-limits-01",
      "prompt": "Evaluate \\(\\lim_{x\\to5}\\frac{x^2-25}{x-5}\\).",
      "answer": "Factor the numerator:\n\\[\nx^2-25=(x-5)(x+5).\n\\]\nFor \\(x\\ne5\\),\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2-25}{x-5}=x+5.\n\\]\nTherefore the limit is\n\\[\n5+5=10.\n\\]",
      "rating": "**",
      "paperTags": ["term-1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "math-i-limits-algebraic-limits-02",
      "prompt": "Evaluate \\(\\lim_{x\\to9}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-3}{x-9}\\).",
      "answer": "Rationalise the numerator:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-3}{x-9}\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{x}+3}{\\sqrt{x}+3}=\\frac{x-9}{(x-9)(\\sqrt{x}+3)}.\n\\]\nFor \\(x\\ne9\\), this is\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+3}.\n\\]\nThus the limit is\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{3+3}=\\frac{1}{6}.\n\\]",
      "rating": "***",
      "paperTags": ["term-1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "math-i-limits-algebraic-limits-03",
      "prompt": "Evaluate \\(\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{(1+h)^3-1}{h}\\).",
      "answer": "Expand:\n\\[\n(1+h)^3-1=1+3h+3h^2+h^3-1=3h+3h^2+h^3.\n\\]\nFor \\(h\\ne0\\),\n\\[\n\\frac{(1+h)^3-1}{h}=3+3h+h^2.\n\\]\nTaking \\(h\\to0\\) gives\n\\[\n3.\n\\]",
      "rating": "***",
      "paperTags": ["term-1"]
    }
  ]
